Title: Wimbledon 2025: Who are the winners of this year's tournament?
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Iga Swiatek', 'Text': '"It seems super surreal," said 24-year-old Iga.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 44}}, {'Speaker': 'Iga Swiatek', 'Text': '"Honestly, I didn\'t even dream of winning Wimbledon because it was way too far.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 16, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 75}}, {'Speaker': 'Iga Swiatek', 'Text': '"I feel like I\'m an experienced player, having won other Slams, but I didn\'t expect this."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 17, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 83}}, {'Speaker': 'Jannik Sinner', 'Text': 'After winning the men\'s title, Jannik thanked Carlos, saying: "It is so difficult to play you, but we have a great relationship off the court."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 28, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 124}}, {'Speaker': 'Jannik Sinner', 'Text': '"Keep going, keep pushing, you are going to hold this trophy many times - you already have twice!"', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 29, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 86}}, {'Speaker': 'Alfie Hewett', 'Text': '"When you lose, to have this amount of love and support, this sort of atmosphere doesn\'t happen to us on a regular basis.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 36, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 113}}, {'Speaker': 'Alfie Hewett', 'Text': '"It is really incredible the amount of support wheelchair tennis has got."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 37, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 68}}], 'Description': [{'Description': "On Saturday, Poland's Iga Swiatek had a decisive victory over USA's Amanda Anisimova - claiming her first Wimbledon Ladies' Singles title.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 111}}, {'Description': 'Both players were competing in their very first Wimbledon final, but Iga took control of the match quickly.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 90}}, {'Description': 'She dominated Amanda with a 6-0 6-0 victory in just 57 minutes.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 12, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 56}}, {'Description': 'Ultimately Jannik Sinner was the winner, following a nail-biting match.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 25, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 65}}, {'Description': "Great Britain's Alfie Hewett returned to defend his Wheelchair Singles title against world number one Tokito Oda.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 33, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 102}}, {'Description': '19-year-old Tokito lost the opening set but went on to win the next two sets, claiming victory.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 34, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 85}}, {'Description': 'Alfie shared his gratitude for the support he received during the match.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 35, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 67}}, {'Description': "Men's Doubles - Britain's Julian Cash and Lloyd Glasspool. You can read more about their victory here", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 43, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 86}}, {'Description': "Women's Doubles - Russia's Veronika Kudermetova and Belgium's Elise Mertens", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 44, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 71}}, {'Description': "Mixed Doubles - The Netherlands' Sem Verbeek and Chechia's Katerina Sin", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 45, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 67}}, {'Description': 'Wheelchair Doubles - Martin de la Puente and Ruben Spaargaren, defeating reigning British champions Alfie Hewett and Gordon Reid', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 46, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 108}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'iga swiatek smiling while holding the wimbledon ladies singles trophy on a balcony at wimbledon'}]}
